/ SUGGESTED INITIALIZATION CODE FOR THE 'USER' COMMANDS:

/	UCMNDS,	CLA STL RTL	/CLEAR AC, SET '+2'
/		CDF 10
/		ISZ I (FORLVL	/REDUCE LOOP COUNT
/		STL RAL
/		JMS I (PCHK	/FIX STACK POINTER

/ THIS DISCARDS INFORMATION SAVED BY THE 'UNTIL' COMMAND,
/LEAVING THE USER COMPLETELY FREE TO INTERPRET THE SUBSE-
/QUENT TEXT IN ANY MANNER.  TO GENERATE A SERIES OF 'SUB-
/COMMANDS' ('U A','U B','U C', ETC.), USE 'SCANLN' TO GET
/THE SECOND LETTER (AND SKIP TO THE NEXT PARAMETER FIELD)
/THEN PUT 'TEMP' IN 'CHAR' AND CALL 'LSORT' TO SELECT THE
/DESIRED COMMAND.  THE ROUTINES 'GETOPT' AND 'GTNAME' MAY
/ALSO BE USEFUL FOR EVALUATING CERTAIN COMMAND OPTIONS...

/ A 'JMP EXIT' INSTRUCTION WILL CONTINUE EXECUTION OF THE
/PROGRAM WHEN THE COMMAND IS FINISHED.


/	LOWER FIELD SORT-AND-BRANCH ROUTINE: 'LSORT'

SORTER,	0
	JMS I IOWAIT	/CLEAR AC, RESET DF, TURN IOF
	TAD I SORTER	/GET LIST ADDRESS
	ISZ SORTER
	DCA AUTO

	TAD CHAR	/CONVERT TO EIGHT-BIT
	AND K177
	TAD LM140	/CHECK FOR LOWER CASE
	SMA
	TAD LM40	/TURN INTO UPPER CASE
	TAD L340
	DCA AUTO 2	/SAVE FOR OTHER CHECKS

	TAD I AUTO
	SPA		/END OF LIST ?
	JMP ERR
	CIA
	TAD AUTO 2
LM140,	SZA CLA		/MATCH ?
	JMP .-6
	TAD AUTO
	TAD I SORTER	/YES: COMPUTE ENTRY POINT
	DCA SORTER
	TAD I SORTER
	DCA SORTER
ERR,	CLA CLL		/NO: FALL THROUGH OFFSET!
	JMP I SORTER	/L=0
/////
/ MULTIPLE-COLUMN OUTPUT ROUTINE FOR DIRECTORY LISTINGS

	*.!177&7740	/TO GET 'L340'
L17,	17		/SPACE MASK
	TAD [CR-SP
